%% Sequence 04c — Resolve review dispute
%% Scenario: system administrator resolves one already-opened dispute case.
%% Evidence status: Implemented; AI advice never replaces human decision.
%% Scope: authoritative resolution. Construction is shown in arch_02b; advisory callback is seq_04e.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as System administrator
    participant C as «boundary» ResolveReviewDisputeController
    participant K as «control» ResolveReviewDisputeCommand
    participant U as «outbound» Resolution unit of work
    participant DB as «store» PostgreSQL + event outbox

    A->>C: POST /api/admin/reviews/disputes/:disputeId/resolve
    C->>K: execute(decision, rationale, selected actions)
    activate K
    K->>U: run atomic resolution
    U->>DB: Lock case, load dossier and actor role
    DB-->>U: Resolution context
    U-->>K: Persistence session
    K->>K: Validate authority, readiness, decision, and actions
    alt Case can resolve
        K->>U: Save resolution, audit, and resolved-event intent
        U->>DB: Commit human decision + audit + durable event
        DB-->>U: Resolved case
        U-->>K: Resolution result
        K-->>C: 201 result with human decision
        C-->>A: Show authoritative outcome
    else Terminal or invalid
        K-->>C: Conflict/business error
        C-->>A: Keep prior state
    end
    deactivate K
    Note over DB: Post-commit consumers process the durable event.\nThey never decide or replace the administrator's resolution.
